  {
    "hotel_id": "100122",
    "hotel_url": "https://www.agoda.com/ana-crowne-plaza-sapporo/hotel/sapporo-jp.html",
    "name": "ANA Crowne Plaza Sapporo By IHG",
    "detail": "I arrived in Sapporo via a free shuttle bus provided by a resort hotel at Lake Toya. The drop off point was just outside Sapporo JR Train Station and it was snowing heavily and temperature was below zero degree. It was impossible to walk on surface road. We got into train station and walk thru underground walkway. To our surprise, the hotel is right outside exit 21. The hotel room has great view of the city, we enjoyed the view of snowing from our room. The room may be small for western standard, but quite spacious for Japanese standard. We enjoyed the breakfast on level 24 with great city view and the Japanese set breakfast was fantastic. There are many good Japanese Reataurants around the hotel and walking distance to many tourist attractions like the Odori Park, clock tower and Former Hokkaido Government Office Buidling, Hokkaido University, etc. We took the last suttle bus to Chitose Airport at 3.30pm and arrived at about 7pm due to heavy snowing, it costs us only 1000 yen per head (again very cheap for Japanese Standard). The hotel's great location provided hassle free transfer to many other Hokkaido tourist attractions, including airport tranfer.",
